---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { site, mailtoLink } from '../site.config';

const email = mailtoLink('Privacy question');
const { address } = site.places;
---

<Base title="Privacy policy" description="How UNBORING PEOPLE handles the little data this site collects, in plain language.">
  <PageHeader eyebrow="Privacy" title="Privacy, in plain words.">
    <p>What this site collects, why, who else sees it, and how to make us delete it. No legalese where we can avoid it.</p>
  </PageHeader>

  <article class="wrap policy">
    <p class="review placeholder">
      [REVIEW: This is a plain-language draft, not legal advice. Have it checked against India's Digital Personal Data
      Protection Act, 2023 and any US state privacy laws that apply before launch.]
    </p>
    <p class="label">Last updated: 3 November 2026</p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name}, {address.street}, {address.city} {address.postalCode}, Gujarat, India. Questions about your data go to
      {email ? <a href={email}>{site.contact.email}</a> : site.contact.email}.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect, and why</h2>
    <h3>The contact form</h3>
    <p>
      If you use the form on our Talk page, we get your name, business, website or Instagram, your message, and your phone
      or email. We use it only to reply to you and, if you hire us, to work with you. The form is run by Netlify, our
      website host, which stores submissions for us.
    </p>
    <h3>WhatsApp and email</h3>
    <p>
      When you message us on WhatsApp or by email, we see what you send. WhatsApp (Meta) and the email providers handle those
      messages under their own privacy policies.
    </p>
    <h3>The Boring Test</h3>
    <p>
      Your answers and score stay in your browser. We don't receive them unless you choose to send them to us, for example by
      tapping the WhatsApp button on your result. The shareable score card is made in your browser and never uploaded by us.
    </p>
    <h3>Analytics and ads</h3>
    <p>
      If you accept our cookie notice, we use Google Analytics 4 to count visits and see which pages work, and the Meta Pixel
      to measure our ads on Facebook and Instagram. Both set cookies and send usage data to Google and Meta. If you decline,
      neither loads. You can change your mind at any time from the link in the footer.
    </p>
    <h3>Things your browser remembers</h3>
    <p>
      To avoid showing you the same joke twice, the site keeps a few small notes in your browser's session storage: whether
      you've seen the intro, how many times you pressed the boring button, and whether boring mode is on. They never leave
      your device and disappear when you close the tab.
    </p>

    <h2>Who else sees it</h2>
    <p>
      Only the services named above: Netlify, Google, Meta (including WhatsApp), and our email provider. We don't sell your
      data. We don't share it with anyone else unless the law requires us to.
    </p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>Messages and form submissions: up to 24 months after our last conversation, unless you ask us to delete them sooner.</p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask us what we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete it. Email us and we'll do it within
      30 days. You can also decline analytics cookies, or clear them in your browser.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If we change this policy, we'll update it here and change the date at the top.</p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .policy {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    max-width: 52rem;
    margin-inline: 0;
    padding-block: var(--section);
  }
  .review { padding: 1rem; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .policy h2 {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    line-height: 1;
  }
  .policy h3 { margin-top: 0.75rem; font-family: var(--font-label); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em; font-size: 1rem; }
  .policy p { max-width: 65ch; }
  .policy a { text-decoration-color: var(--lime); text-decoration-thickness: 3px; font-weight: 700; }
  @media (min-width: 1000px) {
    .policy { margin-left: max(var(--gutter), calc((100vw - var(--max)) / 2 + var(--gutter) + 10%)); }
  }
</style>
